\DOC ACCUMULATOR_POP_ASSUM_LIST

\TYPE {ACCUMULATOR_POP_ASSUM_LIST : ((thm list) -> tactic) -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Removes from the assumption list every "accumulator" assumption — those stating
a word-level carry/sum or multiply-high/low relation as a real-number equation
— and applies a supplied theorem-list tactic to the removed assumptions.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {ttac : (thm list) -> tactic} is run on the list of discharged
accumulator assumptions, taken as theorems; in the observed traces it is used
to drop them ({K ALL_TAC}), to re-add them to the conclusion as a conjoined
antecedent ({MP_TAC o end_itlist CONJ}, optionally after a normalising rule),
or to re-assume them in processed form ({STRIP_ASSUME_TAC o ...}). Applied to
{A ?- t}, the accumulator assumptions are deleted from {A}, the remaining
assumptions keeping their original order, and {ttac} is then run on the deleted
ones. Exactly one subgoal results. Depending on {ttac}, the conclusion is
either left unchanged, or becomes {u ==> t} where {u} is built from the
discharged assumptions (possibly rewritten into a normalised form before being
conjoined); in one case the processed assumptions {z1 ... zp} are put back into
the assumption list in place of the originals while the conclusion stays {t}.
Writing {A'} for the non-accumulator assumptions, this last case is
{
           A ?- t
     ======================  ACCUMULATOR_POP_ASSUM_LIST ttac
        A', z1, ..., zp ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one-subgoal transformation, always on goals
carrying a large set of such accumulator assumptions.

\ENDDOC
